The DTS Coherent Acoustics decoder and core encoder (crates/dts, the rivet-dts
repository, https://github.com/safewords/rivet-dts, under the same
licence as the H.264 / H.265 decoders) are original code by the same author, written from
ETSI TS 102 114 V1.6.1, which ETSI publishes free of charge, with its
normative tables transcribed from that PDF and cross-checked against V1.2.1.
They do not include or derive from any other DTS decoder or encoder (not
libavcodec, not libdcadec); the two code books no ETSI edition prints are not
included. The decoder is checked against its own encoder and, as a black box,
libdca's decoder. DTS Coherent
Acoustics was patented by DTS, Inc.; "DTS" is a trademark of its owner, used
only to name the format.

