The WebP decoder and encoder (crates/webp, the rivet-webp repository,
https://github.com/safewords/rivet-webp, under the same licence as the
H.264 / H.265 decoders) are original code by the same author. The container
parser and writer, the lossless (VP8L) decoder and encoder, the alpha (ALPH)
coding, the animation compositor and encoder and the colour conversion are
written from RFC 9649 (WebP Image Format) and ITU-R BT.601; the lossy (VP8)
bitstream is decoded and encoded by rivet-vp8, above. They do not include or
derive from any other WebP implementation's source: none was read (not
libwebp, not image-rs's image-webp, not any other), and none is run by the
tests. The decoder is checked against Google's public WebP test files and
gallery images (libwebp-test-data and the WebP gallery), used as data and not
distributed. WebP and VP8 are generally offered royalty-free by their
designers; this software grants no patent rights and makes no claim about
whether a licence is needed.

